2026-09-27: bounded K04 observation; the historical stall remains OPEN.

ublk-blocked-observer.c includes the existing selftest-init.c and observes its
wait loop at 25/40/46/58 seconds and before shutdown sync. It requests SysRq
blocked-task stacks, reads the resulting kmsg records, memory/I/O pressure,
and fio/ublk/bash/timeout process wait channels/stacks. It does not change the
original program, workers, error assertions, 45-second upstream timeout or
60-second outer bound. Observations are diagnostic, not a replacement test.

The first subject flight passes. In the first reference flight the original
workload finishes and the boot/shutdown predicate passes, but normal kernel
printk interleaves EVO_BOOT_NONCE. The strict program parser rejects that
capture: INVALID_OUTPUT, not a reference-program PASS. Its raw log is retained.
For the next flights console loglevel is 4 rather than 7; explicit kmsg reads
retain the requested diagnostic without parsing a reconstructed nonce.

Six subsequent pairs on the retained matching Images pass the unchanged
original workload and shutdown: 6/6 GCC and 6/6 EvoCC. Each final snapshot
completes with no blocked tasks; no workload lasts until the 25-second sample.
These observations do NOT reproduce/explain the old stall or repair the kernel.
Do not change historical full-test outcomes or mark K04/K13 complete.

Build in evo-flight-lab:sealed, linux/arm64, network none:
  gcc-14 -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I/harness
    /fixtures/ublk-blocked-observer.c -o /probe/init
  /kernel/usr/gen_init_cpio -t 0 /probe/payload.spec > /probe/payload.cpio
tools/k1/selftest.py flight: hvf-host, KUnit autorun off, explicit QEMU drift.
Per-flight ext4 snapshot backing hashes remain unchanged. No full disk copy,
Image rebuild or module replacement; final initramfs is only 854528 bytes.

